.TH @BINARY@ 1 "@DATE_SHORT@" "@NAME@ @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@BINARY@ \- @DESCRIPTION@
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @BINARY@
[\fB\-\-kiosk\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
@LONG_DESCRIPTION@
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-kiosk
Kiosk mode: fullscreen, a status bar and an on screen keyboard.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the configuration built into this binary.
.TP
.B \-\-meta
Print the package name, version and description.
.TP
.BI \-\-write\-icon " FILE"
Write the built in icon to FILE.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/@ID@/
The remembered setup, trusted server keys and, with the unsafe credential
store, passwords.
.SH SEE ALSO
Built with tacoshell.
